  "id": "cortical-column",
  "term": "cortical column",
  "definition": "A cortical column is a functional unit in the cerebral cortex. In primary visual cortex (V1), it can be understood as a basic unit that processes mapped image patches independently and helps analyze local visual features such as contours, lines, and edges.",
